--- Run note ---
Methods A-D above are verbatim output from a single
`SOLAR_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000 SOLAR_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-local-solar-proxy
SOLAR_MODEL=solar-pro4 ./scripts/verify.sh` run (env -i scrubbed, see
case-01-solar-open2.log for why that is required in this dev
environment). That run was interrupted by the harness partway through
Method E, so Method E was re-issued on its own, with the exact command
the script builds -- including the host.docker.internal rewrite the
script now applies to a loopback SOLAR_BASE_URL, since the host's
127.0.0.1 means nothing inside the container. Its output is recorded
above as it was returned.

Caveat on Method A: it goes through the `claude-upstage` wrapper, which
hardcodes Upstage's own endpoint and does not honor SOLAR_BASE_URL, so
that one check did not exercise the proxy or solar-pro4 -- it is the
wrapper's own default path. The script's header already documents that
it never asserts Method A's model. Methods B, C, D and E all ran
against solar-pro4 through the local bridge.
